From: disco-flying-wing-fpv
Subject: [PATCH] sdkcore: static libc++, 16 KB page alignment

Android 15+ devices may use 16 KB memory pages and refuse native
libraries whose LOAD segments are 4 KB aligned (NDK r21 default), as Play
does for new apps. Link libsdkcore with max-page-size=16384, and link
libc++ statically: libsdkcore is the only C++ library in the app, and the
NDK r21 libc++_shared.so is itself 4 KB aligned.
---
diff --git a/sdkcore/src/main/jni/Application.mk b/sdkcore/src/main/jni/Application.mk
index 4c4fbc7..d4a1179 100644
--- a/sdkcore/src/main/jni/Application.mk
+++ b/sdkcore/src/main/jni/Application.mk
@@ -1,2 +1,5 @@
 APP_PLATFORM := android-24
-APP_STL := c++_shared
+# Disco FPV: static libc++ (libsdkcore is the only C++ library in the app)
+# and 16 KB ELF segment alignment, for Android 15+ devices with 16 KB pages.
+APP_STL := c++_static
+APP_LDFLAGS += -Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384
